// RA3 fixture: the combat terms of the RA3 fixture world, for the tests of armour, warheads and
// weapons (ra3_*.rs; docs/RA2_PARITY_PLAN.md sections 4.3 and 4.4). Fixture data, independent of
// the shipped balance (invariant I10).
//
// Warheads: the bullet harms flesh and does not damage walls or trees; the shell harms
// everything; the blast has a spread of 2 cells with 25 percent at its edge; the flak has a
// spread of 1 cell with 50 percent at its edge and does nothing to concrete; the needle deals 1
// percent to plate and hull (attacked only on order) and nothing to concrete; the torpedo harms
// hulls only; the fallout harms no building; the megaton has a spread of 4 cells with 10 percent
// at its edge.
//
// Weapons: the rifle, the long rifle and the cannons engage the ground only; the mortar bomb
// has a minimum range of 2 cells and flies; the autocannon fires bursts of 3; the sam and the
// flak burst engage aircraft only, the latter scattering up to 2 cells at full range; the flak
// shell flies and scatters up to 1 cell; the rockets engage both layers.
//
// Types: the heavy tank carries the big cannon and the sam, and at elite rank the autocannon
// and the sam; the boat uses its depth charge (secondary) against what is underwater; the sub is
// underwater and attacks nothing on land; the squid is underwater and organic, and uses its
// second weapon against organic targets; the flak car carries the flak shell and the flak burst
// with an air range bonus of 2 cells; the sniper never attacks what is on water; the wall is a
// wall. The seven types of the tests of sub cells and crushing: the recruit, the hazmat, the
// jumper, the truck and the roller are unarmed, the trooper carries the rifle, and the brute
// the sam, which engages aircraft only.
(
    schema_version: 2,
    armour_classes: ["flesh", "plate", "concrete", "hull"],
    warheads: [
        (id: "bullet", cell_spread: 0, percent_at_max: 100, wall: 0, wood: 0, versus: [(armour: "flesh", percent: 100), (armour: "plate", percent: 20), (armour: "concrete", percent: 10), (armour: "hull", percent: 20)]),
        (id: "shell", cell_spread: 0, percent_at_max: 100, wall: 1, wood: 1, versus: [(armour: "flesh", percent: 50), (armour: "plate", percent: 100), (armour: "concrete", percent: 100), (armour: "hull", percent: 100)]),
